      "side": 1,
      "message": "model_limit uses integer floor (pct * fleet // 100), so a small fleet floors to 0 and disables self-scheduling entirely even when a non-zero percentage is configured. E.g. one host at 50% gives limit 0, so that model can never self-schedule; two hosts at 25% also floors to 0. The test pins this as intended, but it contradicts the operator\u0027s intent (50% of one host should allow that one host). Consider ceil, or rounding to nearest with a min of 1 when pct \u003e 0 and fleet \u003e 0.",
      "revId": "99515c918decbeb53408fdf1703fb871f44815b3",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
